<?
$cfg = parse_plugin_cfg('docker.rolling.update');
require_once "$docroot/plugins/dynamix.docker.manager/include/DockerClient.php";
require_once "$docroot/plugins/docker.rolling.update/include/rolling.php";
$ctList = '';   // one checkbox per template container, checked = handled by the rolling update
foreach ((new DockerTemplates())->getTemplates('user') as $t) {
  $x = @simplexml_load_file($t['path']);
  $n = $x ? trim((string)$x->Name) : '';
  if ($n === '') continue;
  $ctList .= "<label style='display:inline-block;min-width:16em;margin:2px 0'><input type='checkbox' class='rolling-ct' value='".htmlspecialchars($n)."'".(rolling_excluded($n, $cfg) ? '' : ' checked')."> ".htmlspecialchars($n).'</label>';
}
?>
<form markdown="1" method="POST" action="/update.php" target="progressFrame" onsubmit="$('#EXCLUDE').val($('.rolling-ct:not(:checked)').map(function(){return this.value}).get().join(','))">
<input type="hidden" name="#file" value="docker.rolling.update/docker.rolling.update.cfg">
<input type="hidden" name="EXCLUDE" id="EXCLUDE" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($cfg['EXCLUDE'] ?? '')?>">

_(Enable the rolling update)_:
: <select name="ENABLED"><?=mk_option($cfg['ENABLED'] ?? 'yes', 'yes', _('Yes'))?><?=mk_option($cfg['ENABLED'] ?? 'yes', 'no', _('No'))?></select>

> No: the Update / Update All buttons of the Docker page behave natively again for every container (pull, stop, remove, recreate: no health gate, no rollback). The plugin stays installed and the settings below are kept. Reload the Docker page after changing this.

_(Containers handled by the rolling update)_:
: <span id="rolling-cts"><?=$ctList ?: '<i>'._('No container templates found').'</i>'?></span>

> Unchecked containers are updated the native way (pull, stop, remove, recreate: no health gate, no rollback). Containers created later are handled by the rolling update until unchecked here. <a href="#" onclick="$('.rolling-ct').prop('checked',true);return false">Select all</a> - <a href="#" onclick="$('.rolling-ct').prop('checked',false);return false">Select none</a>

_(Health gate timeout)_ (seconds):
: <input type="number" name="TIMEOUT" min="5" max="3600" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($cfg['TIMEOUT'] ?? '120')?>">

> Maximum time to wait for the new container to become healthy before rolling back. Per-container override: label `rolling.timeout`.

_(Grace period)_ (seconds):
: <input type="number" name="GRACE" min="1" max="3600" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($cfg['GRACE'] ?? '15')?>">

> For containers without a healthcheck: how long the new container must stay up without restarting. Per-container override: label `rolling.grace`. If grace > timeout, timeout is raised to grace.

_(Notify on successful update)_:
: <select name="NOTIFY"><?=mk_option($cfg['NOTIFY'] ?? 'yes', 'yes', _('Yes'))?><?=mk_option($cfg['NOTIFY'] ?? 'yes', 'no', _('No'))?></select>

> Normal notification when a container was updated and passed its health gate without any warning.

_(Notify on update with warnings)_:
: <select name="NOTIFY_WARNING"><?=mk_option($cfg['NOTIFY_WARNING'] ?? 'yes', 'yes', _('Yes'))?><?=mk_option($cfg['NOTIFY_WARNING'] ?? 'yes', 'no', _('No'))?></select>

> Warning notification when the update succeeded but something was off: invalid label value, probe fallback, blue/green prerequisites missing. The warnings are listed in the notification.

_(Notify on errors)_:
: <select name="NOTIFY_ERROR"><?=mk_option($cfg['NOTIFY_ERROR'] ?? 'yes', 'yes', _('Yes'))?><?=mk_option($cfg['NOTIFY_ERROR'] ?? 'yes', 'no', _('No'))?></select>

> Alert notification on rollback, on a skipped update (image pull failed, template not found, leftover `.rollback` container) and when manual intervention is required.

&nbsp;
: <input type="submit" value="_(Apply)_"><input type="button" value="_(Done)_" onclick="done()">
</form>

### Per-container labels

Edit the container → *Add another Path, Port, Variable, Label or Device* → **Label**.

| Label | Values | Default |
|---|---|---|
| `rolling.strategy` | `safe`, `bluegreen` | `safe` |
| `rolling.probe` | `health`, `running`, `http://host:port/path`, `tcp://host:port`, `none` | `health` if the image has a HEALTHCHECK (or `--health-cmd` in Extra Parameters), otherwise `running` |
| `rolling.timeout` | seconds | global setting |
| `rolling.grace` | seconds | global setting |

**`bluegreen`** (zero-downtime, Traefik Docker provider only) requires: a user-defined bridge network, no host port mapping, no fixed IP, a healthcheck, Traefik labels with an explicit `traefik.http.routers.<r>.service=<s>` and `traefik.http.services.<s>.loadbalancer.server.port=<port>`, Tailscale disabled - and an application that tolerates two instances running on the same data. When a prerequisite is missing the update falls back to safe mode and lists what is missing.
